      {
        "id": 90270,
        "name": "Ronway",
        "username": "Ronway",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/ronway/{size}/1856_2.png",
        "created_at": "2014-02-10T20:43:44.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"Foote\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/foote/48/1877_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Foote:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<div><b>Ronway wrote:</b><br><blockquote>&nbsp;phantaskippy wrote:<br><blockquote>While damage amount is calculated seperately for each instance, the source is not.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;\n&nbsp;\n</blockquote>\nWhere has this been stated? If a link can be provided that the source will not be recalculated, then why hasn't it been done so already? If there is no such link, then why I you saying it like it's a fact?\n</blockquote></div>\nTo be fair, nothing says it does either. There is no other precedent to cite in favor or against. Thats why its being debated in the first place.\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>To be fair, no one has said \"damage amount and the source is calculated seperately for each instance\", where \"damage is recalculated seperately for each instance, the source is not\" has been stated several times in various different ways. Sounds like people who are against the lowest HP Ennead member from changing are using a phrase that has never been confirmed, where the ones who question it are going by the strict wording of the card.</p>",
