      {
        "id": 90273,
        "name": "Foote",
        "username": "Foote",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/foote/{size}/1877_2.png",
        "created_at": "2014-02-10T21:51:57.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"Ronway\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/ronway/48/1856_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Ronway:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>I can't help but think that if they were going for that, they would of worded it more like this;</p>\n<blockquote>Select the Villain target with the lowest HP.That target deals all hero targets X damage.\n&nbsp;\n</blockquote>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>I agree with you here.</p>\n<p>But it is really not that much different than</p>\n<blockquote>\nThe Villain target with the lowest HP deals all hero targets X damage\n</blockquote>\nPut the word \"Select\" at the bigining of that sentence and it basically adds up to the same thing minus a period.&nbsp;\n<p>Doesn't the player still have to identify a single villain target to be the one with the lowest HP? The player is <em>already</em> going through the steps of the way you worded it by 1) selecting the target then 2) having them deal all heros the damage.&nbsp;</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>Here are the possible senarios, some which we have not entertained, but I thought it worth bringing them up in one place.</p>\n<p><strong>Atum is the lowest HP villain with 1 HP. He starts to deal the 3 instances of damage to all heros after playing Elemental Storm. First he hits Ra with Flame Barrier with the first instance, which reacts and kills Atum. Set has 2 HP and is now the lowest. What happens next?</strong></p>\n<p>A) Atum was the damage source and is destroyed, so the entire damage sequence is interupted totally</p>\n<p>B) Set is the next lowest HP villain and will continue to damage Ra with the 2nd and 3rd instance of damage before moving on to the other heros</p>\n<p>C) Set is the next lowest HP villain. Ra is spared the 2nd and 3rd instance of damage from destroying Atum (since destroying the source should interupt damage sequences), but Set will continue to deal damage to the other heros in Atums absence.</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>",
        "post_number": 24,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T03:15:33.071Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
