      {
        "id": 90274,
        "name": "Ronway",
        "username": "Ronway",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/ronway/{size}/1856_2.png",
        "created_at": "2014-02-10T22:02:00.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"Foote\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/foote/48/1877_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Foote:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<div><b>Ronway wrote:</b><br><blockquote>I can't help but think that if they were going for that, they would of worded it more like this;<br><blockquote>Select the Villain target with the lowest HP.That target deals all hero targets X damage.&nbsp;\n&nbsp;\n</blockquote></blockquote></div>\nI agree with you here.But it is really not that much different than\n<br><blockquote>The Villain target with the lowest HP deals all hero targets X damage\n&nbsp;\n</blockquote>\nPut the word \"Select\" at the bigining of that sentence and it basically adds up to the same thing minus a period.&nbsp;\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>They are quite different, one gives a definite result, while the other leads to this long discussion.</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<blockquote>\nDoesn't the player still have to identify a single villain target to be the one with the lowest HP? The player is <em>already</em> going through the steps of the way you worded it by 1) selecting the target then 2) having them deal all heros the damage.&nbsp;&nbsp;\n</blockquote>\nThis would depend on what the official ruling is, wouldn't it? And wouldn't it be best if the wording is as clear as possible?",
