      {
        "id": 90276,
        "name": "Ronway",
        "username": "Ronway",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/ronway/{size}/1856_2.png",
        "created_at": "2014-02-10T22:25:17.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"Foote\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/foote/48/1877_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Foote:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<div><b>Ronway wrote:</b><br><blockquote><blockquote>Doesn't the player still have to identify a single villain target to be the one with the lowest HP? The player is <em>already</em> going through the steps of the way you worded it by 1) selecting the target then 2) having them deal all heros the damage.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;\n&nbsp;\n</blockquote>\nThis would depend on what the official ruling is, wouldn't it?\n</blockquote></div>\nNot nessesarily. Its important for the player to know which member is the lowest incase one was Stun Bolted or Offensive Transmuted. So yes they have to identify the target regardless of the official ruling. I am just saying players are already going through those steps inadvertantly&nbsp;\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>If the ruling is that the source can be changed if the orignal target has been destroyed, then you will not be selecting a target to deal all the damage, you will be selecting a target for each instance of damage. However if you were told to select a target, then that target deals damage, then if that target is destroyed, then the damage would stop. So yes, it is very reliant on the ruling.</p>",
