      {
        "id": 90280,
        "name": "Foote",
        "username": "Foote",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/foote/{size}/1877_2.png",
        "created_at": "2014-02-11T05:29:30.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"phantaskippy\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/phantaskippy/48/1897_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> phantaskippy:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>I don't think the damage will continue.If a villain card dealt the lowest HP target 3 melee and 3 infernal damage and the lowest HP target dies from the melee damage, does the next in line take the infernal damage?Wouldn't that be the same as if Apostate targetted the Highest HP hero target for 3 melee and 3 infernal, but after the melee damage was dealt that target was no longer the higest HP target?The attack doesn't reconfigure mid-attack.&nbsp;But we'll need an official ruling on this one.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>At least thats how I have been playing it.</p>\n<p>So if the highest HP hero target does not change mid effect in that case, it could hold true for the lowest HP villain target for Elemental Storms.&nbsp;</p>\n<p>Does anyone play it where Apostate would target a 2nd hero for the infernal damage?&nbsp;</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>",
